 "note": "site is the kit function that calls Pillow; via is who called it when the site is a method of reelkit.raster.Frame. xy_types are the Python types of the coordinates (float64 is numpy's, a subclass of float). points and coords are the smallest and largest count and value seen. width \"default\" means the call passed none (ImageDraw.line then draws width 1). Pillow turns every coordinate into a C int by truncation toward zero before it draws. cases names the vector files in this folder whose cases reproduce the row (as_used has whole calls at full size besides); an empty list is a call that makes or wraps an image and draws nothing. np.asarray(image) is not a Pillow call and is not listed. The survey starts after the sprites and title close-ups are built: the Pixel Pitch modules the bridge imports for the models paint posters of their own as they load, which no frame shows.",
